<title>BRAZIL: Exxon Corp Brazil unit names new president.</title>
<headline>Exxon Corp Brazil unit names new president.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exxon Corp's Brazilian affiliate Esso Brasileira de Petroleo Ltda has named engineer Richard Dobson as its new president to replace William Jackson, who is retiring, Esso said in a statement.</p>
<p>Dobson, a Canadian civil engineer who joined Exxon in 1969, will take office on Feb 1, the statement said.</p>
<p>Exxon has been in Brazil for 85 years. It distributes and sells fuel at its 2,800 gas stations throughout the country.</p>
<p>The company also produces lubricants in Brazil, where it has a 15 percent market share, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415</p>
